  "note": "Independent re-judgment against RFC 4271 Section 9.2 ('When a BGP speaker receives an UPDATE message from an internal peer, the receiving BGP speaker SHALL NOT re-distribute the routing information contained in that UPDATE message to other internal peers (unless the speaker acts as a BGP Route Reflector [RFC2796]).') after adding emitPrePolicyAdjRIBOut in reactorAPIAdapter.forwardUpdateSection (reactor_api_forward.go) and reactorForwardRSSectionResult (forward_rs.go) for RFC 8671 Section 5.2. In both functions, the added emitPrePolicyAdjRIBOut call runs strictly AFTER the iBGP split-horizon refusal check (isReflected / reflected with neither source nor destination an RR client continues before reaching emitPrePolicyAdjRIBOut), copies the incoming UPDATE payload read-only for BMP pre-policy Adj-RIB-Out observation, and does not alter split-horizon refusal, route-reflector client exceptions, mods, or forwarding dispatch. All three tagged tests and all other cited producers/helpers are byte-identical to the prior enforced audit, so enforced stands with all 36 code bindings preserved.",
